<title>CANADA: Canada Prairies to see rain east, west, sun centre.</title>
<headline>Canada Prairies to see rain east, west, sun centre.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Wednesday were forecast to see rain east and west with sun in the central region, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see thundershowers north and east with highs of 21 to 24 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see mainly sunny skies with highs of 15 to 20 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see rain and highs of 15 to 22 Celsius.</p>
<p>((--Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
